# Environment variables for paper-monitor
#
# Copy this file to .env for local use ONLY:
#   cp .env.example .env
# Then export the variables you need in your shell session:
#   export $(grep -v '^#' .env | xargs)
#
# NEVER commit .env or any file containing real API keys.
# .env is already listed in .gitignore.
#
# For GitHub Actions: add these as repository secrets
#   (Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions).
# For GitHub Codespaces: use Codespaces secrets
#   (github.com/settings/codespaces) so they are injected
#   automatically into every Codespace without touching .env.

# ── Semantic Scholar ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional. Without a key the API still works but with lower rate limits
# (~100 req / 5 min vs 1 req/s with key). On a 429 the script degrades
# gracefully to PubMed + Europe PMC only.
# Obtain at: https://www.semanticscholar.org/product/api
S2_API_KEY=

# ── PubMed / NCBI ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional. Raises the PubMed rate limit from 3 req/s to 10 req/s.
# Obtain at: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/account/
NCBI_API_KEY=

# ── Zotero ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional. Required only if you want the script to push high-score papers
# to a Zotero library. Both values are needed together.
# Obtain at: https://www.zotero.org/settings/keys
ZOTERO_API_KEY=
ZOTERO_USER_ID=
